#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:250
msgid "Request concurrency"
msgstr "Request concurrency"

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:252
msgid "A document is checked one prose range at a time, and a page of prose is hundreds of small ranges — so wall-clock is dominated by request latency rather than by LanguageTool's own work. Up to `max_concurrent_requests` (default `8`) checks are therefore in flight at once."
msgstr "A document is checked one prose range at a time, and a page of prose is hundreds of small ranges — so wall-clock is dominated by request latency rather than by LanguageTool's own work. Up to `max_concurrent_requests` (default `8`) checks are therefore in flight at once."

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:264
msgid "Lower it when pointing at a shared or rate-limited server — the public `api.languagetool.org` in particular. `1` restores strictly serial checking."
msgstr "Lower it when pointing at a shared or rate-limited server — the public `api.languagetool.org` in particular. `1` restores strictly serial checking."

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:267
msgid "Multi-Engine Mode"
msgstr "Multi-Engine Mode"

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:269
msgid "When both Harper and LanguageTool are enabled, they run one after another and their diagnostics overlay. Findings that agree — the same rule over the same byte range — are merged into one report keeping the higher severity, with the suggestions interleaved so each engine's best guess comes before either engine's tail. The two tokenize independently, so a finding whose span differs even by a byte stays separate."
msgstr "When both Harper and LanguageTool are enabled, they run one after another and their diagnostics overlay. Findings that agree — the same rule over the same byte range — are merged into one report keeping the higher severity, with the suggestions interleaved so each engine's best guess comes before either engine's tail. The two tokenize independently, so a finding whose span differs even by a byte stays separate."

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:282
msgid "For non-English languages (e.g. `spell_language: de-DE`), Harper is automatically skipped since it only supports English, and LanguageTool handles all checking."
msgstr "For non-English languages (e.g. `spell_language: de-DE`), Harper is automatically skipped since it only supports English, and LanguageTool handles all checking."

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:286
msgid "Verify the Connection"
msgstr "Verify the Connection"

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:288
msgid "Run a quick check to confirm everything is wired up:"
msgstr "Run a quick check to confirm everything is wired up:"

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:297
msgid "You should see a JSON response with a match for the misspelling \"sentnce\"."
msgstr "You should see a JSON response with a match for the misspelling \"sentnce\"."

#: ../../guide/languagetool-setup.md:299
msgid "In VS Code, open any Markdown file — diagnostics from both Harper and LanguageTool will now appear."
msgstr "In VS Code, open any Markdown file — diagnostics from both Harper and LanguageTool will now appear."

